fix(tool-market): declare judge_setup's close, and guard the class of bug

judge_setup shipped without declaring `close` in its output schema, so every call
was rejected at runtime with additionalProperties:false. That is the second tool in
a row with the same defect (cross_asset lost from/to/first/min/max), and unit tests
cannot see it: they call the pure function and never touch the registered schema.

So the fix is two-part: declare the field, and add a text-level guard that reads
src/index.ts, extracts each tool's declared output properties, and asserts the set
matches exactly what the implementation returns. Four tools covered
(judge_setup, cross_asset, market_structure, audit_energy_decay).

Deliberately a source-text check: the schemas are object literals inside apply(),
so this is the only place the seam can be verified without booting a host.

35 test files, 552 tests.